 "observations": [
  "col_left L5: «sammà» is printed with a grave accent on the final a.",
  "col_left L5-L10: the lines of the entry deqansā are spaced as printed: 12.9-13.0 points between L5, L6 and L7, 16.1-16.2 points between L7, L8 and L9, where the Syriac words with their vowel points need room, and 12.7 points to the Arabic line L10; L11 stands again on the grid of the page.",
  "col_left L7: «Bar ‘Alī» is letter-spaced; its ī has a bar (2.4 by 1.0 points), as has the ē of «*deqansē*» (3.5 by 1.1).",
  "col_left L8: the Syriac word of Bar ‘Alī, «ܕܵܩܹܢܣܵܐ» (dāqēnsā), is printed with East Syriac dot vowels: two dots slanting upwards to the right over the dalath and over the semkath (zqāpā), and two dots slanting downwards to the right under the qoph (zlāmā qšīyā, the angular zlāmā); the dalath has its dot below. The «x» before «saec.» (the tenth century) cannot be told from a lowercase x by its shape or size in this type (5.0 by 5.2 points, as the small-capital x of the numeral of Derenbourg in L11); it is taken as the small-capital numeral.",
  "col_left L9: «Payne-Smith» is letter-spaced. His form of the word, «ܕܳܩܶܢܣܳܐ», is printed with West Syriac (Greek-letter) vowels: zqāpā over the dalath and over the semkath, rbāṣā over the qoph (the same signs as in the glossary, p. 355).",
  "col_left L10: «الكواكب الثابتة» is unvowelled; the point after it stands to the right of the Arabic, at the end of the line in the Latin reading order.",
  "col_left L12: «*Description de l’Égypte*» is printed in italics, with the apostrophe and É.",
  "col_left L15, L28: the marks over the last i of «adh-Dhahabī» and «nawī» are bars (2.0-2.3 by 0.8-1.0 points), measured with macron_audit.py.",
  "col_left L16: «β» is Greek.",
  "col_left L17: «*shu‘batayn*» has the sign of ‘ayn after the u.",
  "col_left L22: «*dhawā’ib*» has the sign of hamza before the i.",
  "col_left L27: «*tecnical*» is printed so (for technical); transcribed as printed.",
  "col_left L44: the H of «Ḥarrān» has its dot below.",
  "col_right L1: the entry dies of the left column goes on here. A speck at the left margin before «187» and a speck between «).» and «—» are not transcribed.",
  "col_right L4: a speck between «et» and «II» is not transcribed.",
  "col_right L7-L10, L28, L29, L45: the guillemets are printed as small solid wedges, as on pp. 366, 370, 374, 377, 381 and 382.",
  "col_right L8: a speck at the left margin before «circuli» is not transcribed.",
  "col_right L14: «AR» is the sign of right ascension, printed as one sort: an italic A joined to an upright R (twice in the line); transcribed AR.",
  "col_right L14, L15: the bracket opened before «i. e.» in L14 is not closed; the entry ends «(adn. 194-195).» in L15; transcribed as printed.",
  "col_right L23, L27, L44: the marks over the i of «ad-Dimashqī», «*tasyīr*» and «al-Battānī» are bars (2.3-3.5 by 1.0-1.2 points), measured with macron_audit.py.",
  "col_right L27: «ἄφεσις» is Greek, with the smooth breathing and the acute on the first α (as on p. 377).",
  "col_right L31: «adp.» is printed so (adpendicem); «F» is upright.",
  "col_right L32, L33: «a pro» at the end of L32 is printed without a hyphen, and the word goes on as «fectione» in L33 (profectione); transcribed as printed.",
  "col_right L36: a speck (1.2 by 1.2 points) under the t of «stellae», 1.5-2.8 points below the baseline, is not transcribed.",
  "col_right L37: a speck (0.6 by 1.0 point) on the baseline between the r and the i of «Cancri» is not transcribed.",
  "col_right L38, L39: «[=» is printed with a long equals sign.",
  "col_right L40: «+ 90°» is printed with a large plus sign; the degree sign is a raised small o.",
  "col_right L46: the entry distantia Lunae goes on on p. 385."
 ],
